@page "/"
@using System.Reflection
@inject IPromptResolverService PromptResolverService

@*
    The landing, and what it is a landing on.

    Two ways in and nothing else, because there are only two: begin a sitting, or bring back a
    file. Reviewing a domain and taking one away are not ways in at all — they are what you do to a
    domain once one exists, and they are reached from the work itself: a finished sitting lets its
    agent into the domain and lands on the review. A landing that also listed them would be a menu
    of pages rather than a way through the work.

    Neither doorway explains itself, because neither needs to: a door labelled "distil an agent"
    that also tells you what distilling an agent is has stopped being a door and become a leaflet.
    What Morgana does with your answers is hers to show once you are inside.

    It still proves what the scaffold exists to establish — the project reference reaches
    Morgana.AI, morgana.json is readable as an embedded resource from here, and the absence of any
    embedded agents.json degrades to agentless mode instead of failing. Nobody comes here to read
    that, so it is one line at the foot.
*@

<div class="alembic-landing">

    <div class="landing-head">
        <div class="vessel">
            <img src="images/alembic.jpg" alt="Morgana's alembic, lit from within" />
        </div>

        <h1>Alembic</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Here Morgana takes life. Yours the shape, hers the spells.</p>
    </div>

    @*
        The icons are drawn here rather than typed. The alchemical characters this used to use
        have no font on most Linux desktops, so they arrived as tofu or as nothing at all — and an
        icon nobody can see is worse than none, because the space is still spent on it.
    *@
    <div class="gateways">

        <a class="gateway primary-gateway" href="interview">
            <svg class="sigil" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"
                 stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M9.3 3h5.4M10.6 3.4v5.2M13.4 3.4v5.2" />
                <circle cx="12" cy="14.6" r="5.9" />
                <path d="M6.6 15.4c1.8 1.4 9 1.4 10.8 0" />
                <path d="M17.6 12.4H20a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v4" />
            </svg>

            <h2>Distil an agent</h2>
            <span class="go">Begin &rarr;</span>
        </a>

        <a class="gateway" href="import">
            <svg class="sigil" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"
                 stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M20.5 12a8.5 8.5 0 1 1-2.6-6.1" />
                <path d="M20.8 3.5V8h-4.5" />
                <path d="M12 7.5V12l3 1.8" />
            </svg>

            <h2>Take up where you left off</h2>
            <span class="go">Upload &rarr;</span>
        </a>

    </div>

    <div class="footnote">
        @if (loadError is not null)
        {
            <span class="bad">Framework layer unreachable: @loadError</span>
        }
        else if (frameworkPrompt is null)
        {
            <span>Resolving the framework layer&hellip;</span>
        }
    </div>

</div>

@code {
    private Records.Prompt? frameworkPrompt;
    private int policyCount;
    private int templateCount;
    private string? loadError;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            frameworkPrompt = await PromptResolverService.ResolveAsync("Morgana");

            List<Records.GlobalPolicy> policies =
                frameworkPrompt.GetAdditionalProperty<List<Records.GlobalPolicy>>("GlobalPolicies");

            policyCount = policies.Count(p => !p.IsInjectionTemplate);
            templateCount = policies.Count(p => p.IsInjectionTemplate);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            loadError = ex.Message;
        }
    }
}
